File Index

/ScriptEditor.test.tsx
Purpose: Trigger/phrase/body editing and delete-button tests.

/ScriptEditor.tsx
Purpose: Single-script form (mob OR room picker per attach kind, trigger list switches to ROOM_SCRIPT_TRIGGERS for room scripts, phrase with per-trigger hint, monospace body, per-kind command vocabulary crib incl. the Phase 12b room warp set) in the shared mb-field layout. Phase G: top of the form gained a SaveAsSnippetButton (features/content) — no natural heading to attach it to like the other three editors, so it sits alone above the first row.

/ScriptsPage.tsx
Purpose: Scripts tab — script list per area (room entries labeled), separate "+ Add mob script"/"+ Add room script" buttons (Phase 12b: room scripts default to an entry-trigger warp), add/delete scripts, live validateScripts feedback, preview-first save/reload. 2026-07-26 (UX polish pass): its hand-rolled toast JSX (identical to Map/Engine/Access/Skills's own copies) was replaced by the shared features/shared/Toast.js component — own toast STATE unchanged, only the rendering moved. deleteScript now requires a window.confirm ("Delete this mob/room script (trigger)?") — was previously the only entity-delete anywhere in the app with NO confirm at all (scripts have no deleteBlockers-equivalent — nothing references a script, so an unblocked confirm is the correct/only gate). ScriptEditor.test.tsx's one integration test through this page needed window.confirm mocked to keep passing. addScript/addRoomScript/deleteScript now each fire a success toast too. Step 5: gained its own local `dirty` flag (this page hand-rolls its own state, not useAreaWorkbench, so it can't reuse isDirty/confirmDiscard directly) set true by setScripts and cleared on successful openArea/doSave; switchArea() wraps the sidebar's area-button handler with the same "you have unsaved changes… discard and switch areas?" confirm wording as everywhere else. Phase G: new `pendingSnippet` prop — a useEffect mirrors addScript/addRoomScript's own default-to-first-target behavior, retargeting the snippet's saved trigger/phrase/body onto the CURRENT area's first mob or room (the snippet's stored mobVnum is almost certainly from a different area, so it's discarded, never reused).

/ScriptsPage.test.tsx
Purpose: (2026-07-26 UX polish pass, new file — ScriptsPage previously had ZERO page-level tests) deleteScript's window.confirm accepted/declined; add/delete success toasts; switching areas while an added-but-unsaved script is pending prompts to confirm (declined keeps it, accepted switches and clears the list).
